            <div xml:id="d299">

                <pb facs="0613" n="489" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg489"/>

                <head>No. 295.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Everett to Mr. Blaine</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-08-29"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 29, 1881</date>.
                        (Received September 15.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 247.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge your
                    instruction No. 340, of the 30th ultimo, as also your telegraphic instruction of
                    the 26th instant, as follows: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Everett</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Chargé, Berlin</hi>:</p>
                        <p>Leave copy Steuben invitation, No. 240, with imperial minister foreign
                            affairs.</p>
                        <p rendition="#right">BLAINE, <hi rendition="#italic">Secretary</hi>.</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <pb facs="0614" n="490" xml:id="pg490"/>
                <p>And to inform you that immediately on receipt of the former I inclosed a copy of
                    it, with a note, to the acting minister of foreign affairs, a copy of which I
                    inclose. The answer will be transmitted to you by cable as soon as received, and
                    I hope to receive from you, in the mean time, some instruction as to the way and
                    time of the conveyance of the invited guests to the United States, in case they
                    accept the invitation.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>H. SIDNEY EYERETT.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d299-a1.xml" xpointer="d299-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
